       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day, which is twice the maximum labeled daily dose of ibuprofen for adults (3,200 mg/day). That dose carries a serious risk of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events.\n\nWhich of these did you mean?\n\n- **400 mg PO four times daily** (1,600 mg/day total)\n- **800 mg PO three times daily** (2,400 mg/day), a common anti-inflammatory dose\n- **800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day), the maximum, usually for short-term use\n- **1600 mg/day** divided some other way\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want and I'll enter it right away. If you do want the original dose, tell me the clinical rationale and I'll add it as a note. I'd still recommend checking it with pharmacy first."
