       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order. Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily is 6,400 mg/day, twice the maximum daily dose. No standard indication supports it, and it puts the patient at real risk of GI hemorrhage, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events. Normal kidney and liver function and no allergies don't change that.\n\nI can enter any of these right away:\n\n- ibuprofen 800 mg PO four times daily (3,200 mg/day, the maximum)\n- ibuprofen 800 mg PO three times daily (2,400 mg/day)\n- ibuprofen 400 mg PO four times daily (1,600 mg/day)\n\nIf you think this patient needs more than the maximum dose, please talk to pharmacy or the attending first. They can enter or approve it through the hospital's override process. I can also help you pick another analgesic or anti-inflammatory plan."
